10:The base React component and design-token library for Gravity UI apps — controls, inputs, overlays, layout, and theming that every other @gravity-ui package builds on.
11-
12-### When to use
13-
14-- Standard application UI: buttons, form controls, modals and popups, menus, tabs, labels, typography, and layout primitives.
15:- The theming foundation of a Gravity UI app: `ThemeProvider`, design tokens, and CSS variables the rest of the `@gravity-ui/*` ecosystem expects to be present.
16-- Simple tabular data via the built-in `Table` component (selection, sorting, row actions).
17-
18-### When not to use
19-
20-- Feature-rich data grids (virtualization, column resizing, grouping, reordering) — use [`@gravity-ui/table`](https://github.com/gravity-ui/table), a separate headless package. It is **not** the same as uikit's `Table` component.
21-- Charts and data visualization — use [`@gravity-ui/charts`](https://github.com/gravity-ui/charts) (`@gravity-ui/chartkit` is the legacy wrapper).
22-- Application navigation shells (aside header, footer, logo) — use [`@gravity-ui/navigation`](https://github.com/gravity-ui/navigation).
23-- Date pickers, calendars, and range controls — use [`@gravity-ui/date-components`](https://github.com/gravity-ui/date-components).
24-- The SVG icon set itself — use [`@gravity-ui/icons`](https://github.com/gravity-ui/icons); uikit only ships the `Icon` renderer.
25-
26-### Common pitfalls
27-
28:- `Button` styling prop is `view`, not `variant` or `color`
29:- **Components render unstyled without setup.** Wrap the app in `ThemeProvider` **and** import `@gravity-ui/uikit/styles/styles.css` (plus `fonts.css`) once at the entry point — both are required.
30-- **`Icon` has no `name` prop.** Pass an imported icon component through `data`: `import {Gear} from '@gravity-ui/icons'; <Icon data={Gear} size={16} />`.
31-- **`theme` values are `light | dark | light-hc | dark-hc | system`.** `system` (the default) follows the OS preference and resolves to `light` or `dark`. There is no `theme="default"`.
32-
33-### Useful docs
34-
35-- [Layout components and spacings](./guides/layout.md)
36:- [Theming, Colors & Branding](./guides/theming.md)
37-- [Typography](./guides/typography.md)
38-
